  << The boxed double plus the java.lang.Double static API as instance methods
     (call as new Double(0.0).parseDouble("2.5")). Bit views
     (doubleToLongBits / longBitsToDouble) are exact IEEE 754 binary64,
     computed arithmetically. toString follows the Java layout (plain decimal
     for 1e-3 <= |d| < 1e7, otherwise computerized scientific d.dddEn) with the
     shortest digit string that reads back to the same double. parseDouble
     accepts the decimal grammar (hex floating literals are not yet read). >>
  static final double MAX_VALUE = 1.7976931348623157E308;
